Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: HTMLparser.c
Line: 4419
Function: htmlParseDocument
Bug type: out-of-bounds-read
CWE: CWE-125
Explanation: The code calls xmlStrncmp(ctxt->input->cur, "<?xm", 4) without ensuring that at least 4 bytes are available in the input buffer at ctxt->input->cur. If the document contains fewer than 4 bytes and the encoding flag is not set, this reads past the end of the buffer. No GROW or equivalent check is performed before this comparison, allowing an out-of-bounds read on truncated inputs.

